comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-05T06:02:29.591Z","harness:codex","text=Duplicate check 2026-08-05: searched all statuses for the exact GH-896 title and for batch item creation, plan materialize, heterogeneous create, commitWorkspaceTransaction, commitItemMutations, structured mutation, atomic create, and forward references. Closed pm-y9hq owns the SDK transaction primitive and closed pm-xm7c owns the existing CLI/MCP JSON batch; neither provides batch-local references or fixes discovery from create/plan. GitHub source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/896"
  "2026-08-05T06:39:37.946Z","harness:codex","Packed npm and Bun acceptance exposed a structured-mutation attribution bypass: pm item mutate resolved an omitted author against literal unknown instead of tracker author_default. Reused closed canonical pm-42p9nk, linked it as discovered_from, and migrated the adapter to the canonical resolveAuthor precedence using live settings; no duplicate item created."
  "2026-08-05T06:42:41.304Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence 2026-08-05: public resolveItemMutationDocument accepts version 1 heterogeneous create/update/close/release documents, derives deterministic prefix-aware ids, resolves forward aliases in targets/hierarchy/dependencies, rejects malformed/duplicate/unknown/cyclic aliases before writes, and returns alias receipts through CLI and MCP. Durable bulk step ids now fingerprint canonical payloads so transaction-id replay mismatch fails. Focused linked run passed 63/63; full repository coverage and lint passed; isolated packed npm/npx and Bun/bunx consumers created mixed Epic/Feature/Decision graphs, read typed edges, and completed a claimed item atomically. Latest npm pm-changelog 2026.8.4 verified and installed."
  "2026-08-05T07:05:20.954Z","harness:codex","CI follow-up 2026-08-05 on PR 901 exact head e98cbdcb3: coverage aggregation exposed new branch gaps and the smokes gate showed commands.item grew from 336 to 516 bytes because item complete became discoverable. Added real malformed-envelope, unknown dependency, graph convergence, release recovery, minimal/default completion, author precedence, and option-variant tests; focused V8 coverage is now 100/100/100/100 for all three changed runtime modules. Refreshed the measured token baseline for the intentional bounded command addition."
  "2026-08-05T07:17:31.695Z","harness:codex","Review follow-up: CodeRabbit identified a valid prototype-chain collision for the allowed alias constructor and a weak CLI parent-resolution assertion. Replaced the alias map with a null-prototype record, added a constructor regression case, and made the CLI test compare the resolved child parent to the actual derived parent id. Focused tests pass 18/18, eslint and typecheck pass, and focused V8 coverage remains 100/100/100/100."
  "2026-08-05T07:29:35.465Z","harness:codex","Exact-head review follow-up: one shared alias grammar now drives declaration validation, dependency substitution, and cycle discovery. Dependency strings containing malformed id=@ references fail with a usage error before tracker mutation instead of persisting a literal target. The public-surface acknowledgement rationale now matches its package_version semantics. Focused SDK/release suites pass 45/45; typecheck, ESLint, and SDK surface verification pass."
  "2026-08-05T07:40:45.027Z","harness:codex","DeepScan exact-head finding 231630911: the test cast optional mock.lastCall access directly to a committed payload. Added an explicit undefined guard before reading the call argument, so a missing commit fails with a precise test error and static nullability is preserved. Focused test passed 7/7; ESLint and full typecheck passed."
  "2026-08-05T08:39:24.320Z","harness:codex","Evidence: delayed exact-head review corrections are implemented: durable history-first release recovery, exhaustive typed dispatch, executable SDK example, and synchronized contracts. Focused recovery/CLI/release tests passed 60/60; full repository coverage passed 6,864 tests across 433 files at 100% statements, branches, functions, and lines; ESLint, duplicate detection, typecheck, docs links/skills, SDK surface, and contracts checks passed."
  "2026-08-05T08:46:38.043Z","harness:codex","Final local acceptance 2026-08-05: built CLI in unrelated temp Git workspace atomically created Epic/Feature items with deterministic aliases, resolved parent and implements references, claimed the child, and completed it with lock TTL 45s / wait 900ms. Readback proved closed lifecycle, full resolution evidence, dependency/parent graph, and released claim."
